& \Rightarrow & \frac{d}{d x}\left(\frac{f(x)}{x^2}\right) & =-\frac{1}{x^4} \\
\Rightarrow & & f(x) & =c x^2+\frac{1}{3 x} \text{ also } f(1)=1 \Rightarrow c=\frac{2}{3} . \\
& \text{ Hence, } & f(x) & =\frac{2}{3} x^2+\frac{1}{3 x}
\end{aligned}
$$

